    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1302">

                <pb facs="1036" n="920" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg920"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/3566.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.—Paraphrases.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-04-11T21:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 11, 1912—9 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I am informed through respectable sources that a signed organization of 10,000
                    men exists in the State of Vera Cruz to act in cooperation with the rebels in
                    the north, and that as soon as the American railway servants go out they expect
                    to begin destroying bridges and killing Mexican railway employees on the
                    Interoceanic and Mexican railways.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
